cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Ancient Wisdom Atlas — the corpus, the extraction records,
  the motif taxonomy, the indexes, or the findings — please cite it as below.
  Attribution is warmly appreciated even where the CC0 license does not
  require it.
type: dataset
title: "Ancient Wisdom Atlas: a source-grounded atlas of humanity's shared story-patterns"
abstract: >-
  A programmatic, falsifiable atlas of recurring motifs across the sacred and
  traditional literature of the world: 338 public-domain texts across 106
  traditions cleaned into a canonical machine-readable corpus; ~52,600
  evidence-anchored extraction records in which every claim points at a
  verbatim quoted line; a curated taxonomy of canonical motif families; and
  preregistered statistical tests with permutation nulls — including the crown
  experiment, which shows that independently-built, blind taxonomies of the
  connected Old World and of isolated lineages (Australian, Arctic, Amazonian,
  the Americas) share co-occurrence structure well beyond chance. Negative
  results are published alongside positive ones.
